* =============================================================================
* 1.8V I/O LDO Regulator - TI TPS7A8400
* =============================================================================
* Specifications:
*   VIN = 3.3V (from 3.3V buck pre-regulator)
*   VOUT = 1.8V
*   IOUT = 2A
*   Dropout: 200mV max
*   PSRR: >60dB @ 1kHz
*   Output capacitor: 10uF ceramic
* =============================================================================

.title "1.8V I/O LDO Regulator - TPS7A8400 - 1.8V @ 2A"

* =============================================================================
* PARAMETERS
* =============================================================================
.param VIN      = 3.30         ; Input voltage (V)
.param VOUT     = 1.80         ; Output voltage (V)
.param IOUT_NOM = 2.0          ; Nominal output current (A)
.param IOUT_MAX = 2.5          ; Maximum output current (A)
.param VDO_MAX  = 0.20         ; Maximum dropout voltage (V)
.param PSRR_1K  = 60           ; PSRR at 1kHz (dB)

* Reference voltage
.param VREF     = 0.80         ; Internal bandgap reference (V)

* Output capacitor
.param COUT     = 10u          ; Output capacitance (F)
.param COUT_ESR = 5m           ; Output capacitor ESR (ohms)

* =============================================================================
* INPUT SOURCE
* =============================================================================
* 3.3V input from pre-regulator
VIN VIN 0 DC {VIN}

* Input decoupling
CIN1 VIN 0 1u
CIN2 VIN 0 100n

* Input source resistance
RIN_SRC VIN VIN_INT 50m

* =============================================================================
* TPS7A8400 LDO MODEL
* =============================================================================
* The TPS7A8400 is a low-noise, high-PSRR LDO with:
* - Ultra-low noise: 4.4uVrms (10Hz to 100kHz)
* - High PSRR: 60dB at 1kHz
* - Fast transient response
* - Programmable soft-start

* Enable pin
VEN EN 0 DC 5

* Bandgap reference (ideal voltage source with noise)
VREF_BG VREF_NODE 0 DC {VREF}

* Error amplifier (transconductance amplifier)
* gm = 200uS typical
G_EA VIN_INT EA_OUT VREF_NODE FB 200u

* Error amplifier compensation
C_EA EA_OUT 0 10p
R_EA EA_OUT EA_INT 1Meg
C_EA2 EA_INT 0 1p

* Feedback network
* VOUT = VREF * (1 + R1/R2)
* 1.8 = 0.8 * (1 + R1/R2) -> R1/R2 = 1.25
R_FB1 VOUT FB 12.5k
R_FB2 FB 0 10k

* Pass element (PMOS) - modeled as VCCS
* The PMOS is driven by the error amplifier
* Output impedance modeled separately
G_PASS VIN_INT VOUT_INT EA_OUT 0 10

* Pass element output resistance (varies with load)
* Rds(on) at 2A with 200mV dropout: R = VDO/IOUT = 200m/2 = 100mOhm
R_PASS VOUT_INT VOUT_DYN 100m

* =============================================================================
* OUTPUT STAGE
* =============================================================================
* Output capacitor
COUT VOUT_DYN 0 {COUT} Rser={COUT_ESR}

* Additional ceramic caps for stability
COUT2 VOUT_DYN 0 1u Rser=2m
COUT3 VOUT_DYN 0 100n Rser=10m

* Output node connection
R_OUT_SENSE VOUT_DYN VOUT 1m

* =============================================================================
* LOAD
* =============================================================================
* Static load
I_LOAD DC VOUT 0 {IOUT_NOM}

* Dynamic load step for transient analysis
I_LOAD_TRAN VOUT 0 PWL(
+ 0 0
+ 500u 0
+ 510u 0.5
+ 2m 0.5
+ 2.01m 2.0
+ 5m 2.0
+ 5.01m 0.2
+ 8m 0.2
+ 8.01m 2.0
+ 10m 2.0
+)

* =============================================================================
* PSRR TEST SOURCE
* =============================================================================
* AC source on input for PSRR measurement
VIN_AC VIN_AC 0 AC 1
RIN_AC VIN_AC VIN_INT 1m

* =============================================================================
* CURRENT LIMIT
* =============================================================================
* Internal current limit at 2.5A
B_ILIM ILIM 0 V=I(VIN)>{IOUT_MAX} ? 5 : 0

* =============================================================================
* THERMAL SHUTDOWN
* =============================================================================
* Internal thermal shutdown at 165C
RTH_J VOUT TH_J 100
CTH_J TH_J 0 1n
B_TSD TSD 0 V=V(TH_J)>165 ? 5 : 0

* =============================================================================
* ANALYSIS COMMANDS
* =============================================================================
* Operating point
.OP

* Transient analysis for startup and load step
.TRAN 0 10m 0 1n UIC

* AC analysis for PSRR and stability
.AC DEC 100 1 10Meg

* Save key waveforms
.SAVE V(VOUT) V(VIN) I(VIN) V(FB) I(I_LOAD)

* =============================================================================
* DESIGN NOTES
* =============================================================================
* LDO Selection Rationale:
* - TPS7A8400 chosen for high PSRR (>60dB at 1kHz)
* - Low noise critical for sensitive I/O interfaces
* - Fast transient response for digital switching
*
* Dropout Voltage:
* - VIN = 3.3V, VOUT = 1.8V gives 1.5V headroom
* - Dropout requirement: 200mV max easily satisfied
* - Allows operation even with VIN at 2.0V
*
* Stability:
* - 10uF ceramic output capacitor required for stability
* - ESR must be low (<100mOhm) for ceramic caps
* - Additional 1uF and 100nF for high-frequency decoupling
*
* Power Dissipation:
* - Pdiss = (VIN - VOUT) * IOUT = (3.3 - 1.8) * 2 = 3.0W
* - Thermal resistance junction-to-ambient: 35C/W (with copper)
* - Temperature rise: 3W * 35 = 105C
* - Requires thermal pad connection and adequate copper
*
* PSRR:
* - At 1kHz: >60dB means <0.1% of input ripple reaches output
* - Critical for noise-sensitive digital interfaces
* =============================================================================

.END
